"vaiyishlach-","H7971","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he sent"],["לוֹ","lo","H9033","HR/Sp3ms","to him"],["חוּרָם","churam","H2361","HNpm","Huram"],["בְּיַד","beyad-","H3027","HR/Ncbsc","by [the] hand of"],["עֲבָדָיו","'avadav","H5650","HNcmpc/Sp3ms","servants his"],["אֳנִיּוֹת","'oniyot","H591","HNcfpa","ships"],["וַעֲבָדִים","va'avadim","H5650","HC/Ncmpa","and servants"],["יוֹדְעֵי","yod'ei","H3045","HVqrmpc","[who] knew"],["יָם","yam","H3220","HNcmsa","<of> [the] sea"],["וַיָּבֹאוּ","vaiyavo'u","H935","Hc/Vqw3mp","and they went"],["עִם","'im-","H5973","HR","with"],["עַבְדֵי","'avdei","H5650","HNcmpc","[the] servants of"],["שְׁלֹמֹה","shelomoh","H8010","HNpm","Solomon"],["אוֹפִירָה","'ofirah","H211","HNpl/Sd","Ophir towards"],["וַיִּקְחוּ","vaiyikchu","H3947","Hc/Vqw3mp","and they took"],["מִשָּׁם","misham","H8033","HR/D","from there"],["אַרְבַּע","'arba'-","H702","HNcbsa","four"],["מֵאוֹת","me'ot","H3967","HNcfpa","hundred<s>"],["וַחֲמִשִּׁים","vachamishim","H2572","HC/Ncmpa","and fifty"],["כִּכַּר","kikar","H3603","HNcfsc","talent[s] of"],["זָהָב","zahav","H2091","HNcmsa","gold"],["וַיָּבִיאוּ","vaiyavi'u","H935","Hc/Vhw3mp","and they brought [it]"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["הַמֶּלֶךְ","hamelekh","H4428","HTd/Ncmsa","the king"],["שְׁלֹמֹה","shelomoh","H8010","HNpm","Solomon"]],"x":[[14009010,14009010,4],[14009013,14009013,3]],"xn":2}},"people":[{"id":"solomon_2762","name":"Solomon","also":"Jedidiah","summary":"Peaceful, (Heb. Shelomoh), David’s second son by Bathsheba, i.e., the first after their legal marriage (2 Sam. 12). He was probably born about B.C. 1035 (1 Chr. 22:5; 29:1).","verses":273,"father":"David","mother":"Bathsheba","v":[1,2,3,6,8,9,10,11,12,16,17,18]},{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[2,8,9]},{"id":"hiram_1532","name":"Hiram","also":"Huram","summary":"Also “Huram” and “Horam,” king of Tyre. He entered into an alliance with David, and assisted him in building his palace by sending him able workmen, and also cedar-trees and fir-trees from Lebanon (2 Sam. 5:11; 1 Chr. 14:1).","verses":23,"father":"Huram","mother":"","v":[2,18]},{"id":"david_994","name":"David","also":"","summary":"Beloved, the eighth and youngest son of Jesse, a citizen of Bethlehem. His father seems to have been a man in humble life. His mother’s name is not recorded.","verses":896,"father":"Jesse","mother":"","v":[11,14]},{"id":"pharaoh_2332","name":"Pharaoh","also":"","summary":"The Pharaoh of 1 Kings 11:18-22.","verses":9,"father":"","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"daughter_of_pharaoh_989","name":"Daughter of Pharaoh","also":"","summary":"The wife of Solomon (1 Kings 3:1).","verses":5,"father":"Pharaoh","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"moses_2108","name":"Moses","also":"","summary":"Drawn (or Egypt. mesu, “son;” hence Rameses, royal son). On the invitation of Pharaoh (Gen. 45:17-25), Jacob and his sons went down into Egypt.","verses":774,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[13]},{"id":"esau_1216","name":"Esau","also":"Edom, Edomite","summary":"Hairy, Rebekah’s first-born twin son (Gen. 25:25). The name of Edom, “red”, was also given to him from his conduct in connection with the red lentil “pottage” for which he sold his birthright (30, 31).","verses":151,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[17]}],"places":[{"id":"hamath-zobah_517","name":"Hamath-zobah","kind":"","lat":35.1362,"lon":36.74949,"summary":"Fortress of Zobah, (2 Chr. 8:3) is supposed by some to be a different place from the foregoing; but this is quite uncertain.","verses":1,"v":[3]},{"id":"hamath_516","name":"Hamath","kind":"City","lat":35.1359,"lon":36.7495,"summary":"Fortress, the capital of one of the kingdoms of Upper Syria of the same name, on the Orontes, in the valley of Lebanon, at the northern boundary of Palestine (Num. 13:21; 34:8), at the foot of Hermon (Josh. 13:5) towards Damascus (Zech. 9:2; Jer. 49:23).","verses":23,"v":[4]},{"id":"tadmor_1131","name":"Tadmor","kind":"City","lat":34.55405,"lon":38.2659,"summary":"Palm, a city built by Solomon “in the wilderness” (2 Chr. 8:4). In 1 Kings 9:18, where the word occurs in the Authorized Version, the Hebrew text and the Revised Version read “Tamar,” which is properly a city on the southern border of Palestine and toward the wilderness (comp. Ezek. 47:19; 48:28).","verses":1,"v":[4]},{"id":"beth-horon_733","name":"Beth-horon","kind":"City","lat":31.87893,"lon":35.12357,"summary":"House of the hollow, or of the cavern, the name of two towns or villages (2 Chr. 8:5; 1 Chr. 7:24) in the territory of Ephraim, on the way from Jerusalem to Joppa.","verses":4,"v":[5]},{"id":"baalath_137","name":"Baalath","kind":"City","lat":31.92745,"lon":35.05538,"summary":"A town of the tribe of Dan (Josh. 19:44). It was fortified by Solomon (1 Kings 9:18; 2 Chr. 8:6).","verses":2,"v":[6]},{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[6]},{"id":"lebanon_720","name":"Lebanon","kind":"Region","lat":33.92154,"lon":35.89897,"summary":"White, “the white mountain of Syria,” is the loftiest and most celebrated mountain range in Syria. It is a branch running southward from the Caucasus, and at its lower end forking into two parallel ranges, the eastern or Anti-Lebanon, and the western or Lebanon proper.","verses":56,"v":[6]},{"id":"edom_357","name":"Edom","kind":"Region","lat":31.25,"lon":34.75,"summary":"Idumea (Isa. 34:5, 6; Ezek. 35:15). “The field of Edom” (Gen. 32:3), “the land of Edom” (Gen. 36:16), was mountainous (Obad. 1:8, 9, 19, 21).","verses":79,"v":[17]},{"id":"eloth_375","name":"Eloth","kind":"","lat":29.5285,"lon":35.00573,"summary":"","verses":3,"v":[17]},{"id":"ezion-geber_423","name":"Ezion-geber","kind":"City","lat":29.53068,"lon":35.0,"summary":"The giant’s backbone (so called from the head of a mountain which runs out into the sea), an ancient city and harbour at the north-east end of the Elanitic branch of the Red Sea, the Gulf of Akabah, near Elath or Eloth (Num. 33:35; Deut. 2:8).","verses":7,"v":[17]},{"id":"ophir_911","name":"Ophir","kind":"Region","lat":27.5,"lon":67.5,"summary":"Some region famous for its gold (1 Kings 9:28; 10:11; 22:48; Job 22:24; 28:16; Isa. 13:12). In the LXX. this word is rendered “Sophir,” and “Sofir” is the Coptic name for India, which is the rendering of the Arabic version, as also of the Vulgate.","verses":10,"v":[18]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[1961,7093,7093,7093,6242,6242,6242,8141,834,834,8010,1129,1129,1004,1004,3068,3068,3068,853,1004,1004,1004],[8010,1129,5892,5892,2361,5414,5414,8010,3427,3427,1121,8033],[8010,8010,1980,2578,2578,2388,2388,5921],[1129,1129,8412,4057,4057,4057,853,853,3605,3605,4543,4543,5892,834,1129,1129,1129,2574,2574],[1129,1129,5945,8481,8481,1032,4692,4692,5892,2346,2346,1817,1280,1280],[853,853,853,1191,3605,4543,4543,5892,834,1961,1961,8010,853,3605,5892,5892,7393,7393,7393,853,6571,8010,2836,1129,1129,3389,3389,3844,3605,3605,776,776,4475,4475,4475],[3605,3605,3605,5971,5971,3498,3498,4480,2850,2850,567,6522,2340,2983,2983,834,834,3808,3808,3478],[1121,1121,834,3498,776,776,776,834,834,1121,1121,3808,3808,3615,5927,5927,5927,4522,4522,4522,4522,5704,5704,5704,5704,3117,2088],[4480,8010,3808,3808,5414,3478,3478,3478,3478,5650,5650,4399,3588,1992,1992,582,582,4421,4421,8269,8269,8269,7991,7991,8269,8269,8269,7393,7393,7393,6571,6571],[428,8269,8269,8269,8269,5333,4428,4428,8010,2572,7287],[8010,5927,1323,1323,6547,6547,5892,5892,5892,5892,1732,1732,1004,1004,1004,1129,1129,1129,0,0,3588,55